From: Dat Tran <t.ng.t.dat@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: st: stm32mp257f-dk: BME280 on i2c8

ST keeps i2c8 disabled: it is only wired to the GPIO expansion connector
(PZ3 SDA pin 3, PZ4 SCL pin 5). Turn it on and add a Bosch BME280 at
0x76 (its SDO pin tied to GND), handled by the bmp280 IIO driver.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific hardware on the expansion connector]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp257f-dk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp257f-dk.dts
@@ -487,10 +487,16 @@
 	i2c-scl-rising-time-ns = <185>;
 	i2c-scl-falling-time-ns = <20>;
 	clock-frequency = <100000>;
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 	/* spare dmas for other usage */
 	/delete-property/dmas;
 	/delete-property/dma-names;
+
+	/* BME280 on the GPIO expansion connector: SDA pin 3, SCL pin 5, SDO to GND */
+	pressure@76 {
+		compatible = "bosch,bme280";
+		reg = <0x76>;
+	};
 };
 
 &i2s2 {
